  "name": "Question 5",
  "problem": "$4-2.5=${{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "To subtract $2.5$ from $4,$ we break up $2.5$ into its whole number part ($2$) and its decimal part ($0.5$) and proceed in two steps.\n\n- We start at $4$ on the number line and move $2$ places to the left, which brings us to $2.$\n\n- Then, we move the remaining $0.5$ places to the left, leaving us at $1.5.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14149078/assets/7a8da5cb86ba9b216f854161c9be51fbd394a3b7e218fdb2fe4d56891ab258a9.png)\n\nThis gives $4-2.5=1.5.$",
